  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Wednesday...\n\nAbove normal temperatures and dry conditions are expected through\nMonday. Temperatures will be in the high 50s to high 60s F for \nmost locations. The exception will be Carter and Fallon Counties \nwhere high temperatures are expected to be in the high 40s to \nhigh 50s F through Saturday as high pressure lingers in the \nDakotas. This high pressure will set up a strong pressure \ngradient, which when combined with 30-40 kt 850 mb winds Friday \nand Saturday, will lead to 30-45 mph southerly winds east of \nRosebud County. \n\nEnsemble systems are indicating the potential for cooler and\nwetter conditions for the middle of next week. It is too early to\ntalk about too many of the details with this system as it is \nabout a week out. However, there is currently a 30-40% chance of \ngetting greater than 0.25 inches of precipitation. At this time it\nappears that cooler conditions could mean high temperatures in \nthe 40s F for the middle to late week period. Torgerson",
